---
description: SQS, Inbox and Outbox rules
alwaysApply: false
---
- SQS delivery is at-least-once.
- Consumers must be idempotent.
- Use persistent Inbox deduplication.
- ACK messages only after the database transaction commits.
- Business errors are terminal.
- Transient errors must be retried.
- Messages exceeding the retry limit go to the DLQ.
- Financial events must be stored in the Outbox in the same transaction as the financial operation.
- Never publish an event before the financial transaction commits.
- The Outbox Worker publishes pending events.
- Duplicate event publication must remain safe for consumers.